l","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{U}","name":"Wonder","oracle_id":"232284f7-c623-4895-9ab9-8b1a39926830","oracle_text":"Flying\nAs long as this card is in your graveyard and you control an Island, creatures you control have flying.","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2025-04-11","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Incarnation"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{G}","name":"Generic Graveyard Mana Observer","oracle_id":"fixture:graveyard-mana-condition","oracle_text":"As long as this card is in your graveyard and you control an Island, lands you control have \"{T}: Add {G}.\"","power":"1","produced_mana":["B","G","R","U","W"],"released_at":"2015-07-17","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Human Druid"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature with renown deals combat damage to its controller because that damage was redirected, renown will trigger.","oracle_id":"ae42fa8a-b0f6-43dc-a4c6-e2531890ca3a","published_at":"2015-06-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a renown ability triggers, but the creature leaves the battlefield before that ability resolves, the creature doesn\u2019t become renowned. Any ability that triggers \u201cwhenever a creature becomes renowned\u201d won\u2019t trigger.","oracle_id":"ae42fa8a-b0f6-43dc-a4c6-e2531890ca3a","published_at":"2015-06-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Renown won\u2019t trigger when a creature deals combat damage to a planeswalker or another creature. It also won\u2019t trigger when a creature deals noncombat damage to a player.","oracle_id":"ae42fa8a-b0f6-43dc-a4c6-e2531890ca3a","published_at":"2015-06-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect causes Dress Down to become a creature, it will lose its own abilities along with all other creatures. This includes the triggered ability that causes it to be sacrificed at the beginning of the end step.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect grants a creature an ability after Dress Down has entered the battlefield, it won't lose that ability. For example, if a land becomes a creature while Dress Down is on the battlefield, it will still gain any abilities given to it by the effect that animated it. It will, however, lose any abilities it already had.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won\u2019t return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an Aura is put onto the battlefield without being cast, the Aura\u2019s controller-to-be chooses what it will enchant as it comes back onto the battlefield. An Aura put onto the battlefield this way doesn\u2019t target anything (so it could be attached to an opponent\u2019s permanent with hexproof, for example), but the Aura\u2019s enchant ability restricts what it can be attached to. If the Aura can\u2019t legally be attached to anything, it remains in its current zone.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it\u2019s considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners\u2019 graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The timestamp for the \"in your graveyard\" ability is set at the time that this card goes to your graveyard, regardless of whether you control a Mountain at that time.","oracle_id":"eaabd151-2160-4bff-82c0-3fa88659be98","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any permanent can be targeted by the second ability, not just one with counters on it.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Vampire Hexmage's ability can't target a permanent card in a zone other than the battlefield, such as a suspended card.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
